1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,214
A SAFE, or Simple Agreement for
Future Equity, is a contract that

2
00:00:04,214 --> 00:00:08,415
may give an investor equity later
if a specified event occurs.

3
00:00:08,415 --> 00:00:11,740
It is not the same as owning
common stock today, and it is

4
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:15,451
generally not a loan that promises
repayment with interest.

5
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:17,835
The SAFE’s exact terms control.

6
00:00:17,835 --> 00:00:22,216
Some convert during a qualifying
equity financing; others describe

7
00:00:22,216 --> 00:00:24,910
what happens during a sale or
shutdown.

8
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:28,892
A trigger may never occur, so a
SAFE may never convert.

9
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:32,603
Even if it converts, the number
and class of shares depend on the

10
00:00:32,603 --> 00:00:35,348
contract and later capitalization.

11
00:00:35,348 --> 00:00:38,827
Read the triggering events,
valuation cap, discount,

12
00:00:38,827 --> 00:00:43,222
conversion mechanics, and any
treatment in a sale or dissolution.

13
00:00:43,222 --> 00:00:46,186
Do not translate a cap into a
guaranteed ownership

14
00:00:46,186 --> 00:00:47,423
percentage.

15
00:00:47,423 --> 00:00:51,211
A SAFE can be simple in name but
still have important legal and

16
00:00:51,211 --> 00:00:52,990
economic details.

17
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:55,747
Compare it with other
outstanding SAFEs and future

18
00:00:55,747 --> 00:01:00,696
financing plans, and get qualified
advice if the language is unclear.

